## Metadata
Title: FUN'S Cross-Word Puzzles
Author: Evangeline Kearney
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-03-08
Number: 12
Notes: A 13-wide diamond with a shaded cross in the centre printed "No 12" (shown as _), the same template as No. 11, under the heading "FUN'S CROSS-WORD PUZZLES" and the words "Can You Solve Them?" drawn beside the grid. The number is printed in the centre block and in the intro ("the twelfth in FUN'S series"). Credit as printed: "Today's cross work puzzle, the twelfth in FUN'S series, was sent in by Miss Evangeline Kearney of 207 Winthrop street, Brooklyn." Read by hand from the Milwaukee Sentinel's page (Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_03_08_82.png), solution from Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_03_15_86.png, by Claude, 2026-11-16.


